// Title: Msxsl.EXE Execution
// Sigma ID: 9e50a8b3-dd05-4eb8-9153-bdb6b79d50b0
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Timur Zinniatullin, oscd.community
// Date: 2019-10-21 | Modified: 2023-11-09
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1220
// Description: Detects the execution of the MSXSL utility. This can be used to execute Extensible Stylesheet
//   Language (XSL) files. These files are commonly used to describe the processing and rendering of
//   data within XML files. Adversaries can abuse this functionality to execute arbitrary files while
//   potentially bypassing application whitelisting defenses.
// False positives:
//   - Msxsl is not installed by default and is deprecated, so unlikely on most systems.
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1220/T1220.md
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/Msxsl/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_msxsl_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\msxsl.exe"
